  1. [✔] Row one
  First row. The driver sends Space here, then Down, then Space again, so rows one and two should both come back ticked
  in the captured frame while row three stays clear. That contrast is the whole point of the capture: it shows the
  ticked glyph, the unticked glyph, and the cursor glyph in one frame.
❯ 2. [✔] Row two
  Second row. Ticked by the driver as above. Having two adjacent ticked rows also shows whether the renderer marks a run
  of them any differently from a single one.
  3. [ ] Row three
  Third row, deliberately left unticked so the frame carries both states. If every row were ticked the capture could not
  show which glyph means what.
